WEBVTT

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:29.020
You're lookin' a bit pale.

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:33.230
Long trip? Nomad?

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:35.520
Stop asking so many questions.

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:39.440
Fine, fine. Try coming back around six.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:41.400
The waiting room's over there.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.770
You can head right in from the back.

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:55.150
Wanna try entering?

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:59.310
If you win, you won't have to worry about
getting in the ring again for a while.

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:01.940
Hell, you may never get
in another ring again.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.310
Not interested.

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:06.940
Good.

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:11.400
You should forget about dreams
if you wanna see yourself get old.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.190
Hey!

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:31.350
Shit!

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:34.980
He got you good.

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:40.690
That lot's nothin' but trouble. No one
told them they could live over there.

00:01:40.690 --> 00:01:44.480
Someone should chase them
right back to their own country.

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:59.400
There's a community of immigrants
right outside the city.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:02.310
You might find your bike if you go there.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:30.920
MEGALOBOX 2

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:42.310
This is awesome!

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:47.270
Let's see... Now just for
some soap and cough drops.

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:53.480
Get whatever you guys want. It's on me.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:54.690
Yeah!

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:57.020
Well, look at you, Mr. Big Shot.

00:03:57.020 --> 00:04:00.310
Whaddya steal this time?

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:01.850
Top secret, my friend.

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:08.520
You do business with
those immigrants, old man?

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:12.770
I'll happily do business with anyone
as long as they can pay.

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:15.270
The customer's always right.

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:17.770
You dumbass.
You mean money's always right.

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:20.810
Looks like you're quite
acquainted with one yourself.

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:24.270
Nah, he's different. He's one of us.

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:42.690
Look at 'em go!

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:49.900
Yeah, you go back into hiding.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:57.190
Where the hell's my bike?

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:58.650
Who the hell are you?

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:03.400
Let's get outta here, man.

00:05:04.730 --> 00:05:07.770
Wha-- Hey!

00:05:07.770 --> 00:05:08.980
Wait!

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:32.350
What's going on here?

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:35.230
I came to take back
the bike this kid stole.

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:36.730
Stole?

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:45.150
I told you to never do that again!

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:56.730
Stripping these down is easy,
but it'll take some time to restore it.

00:05:56.730 --> 00:05:58.310
Where's the Gear?

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:00.230
I sold it.

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:02.650
Got jack shit for it, though.

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:05.230
Ow!

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:07.150
I'll pay you back for your Gear.

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:10.980
As for your bike, I'll make
sure he fixes it up for you.

00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:12.350
Huh? Me?!

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:16.190
Of course, you. This doesn't
just concern you, you know.

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:20.650
People are gonna say some immigrant stole
something again and blame all of us!

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:23.440
I'm <i>me</i> ! Don't lump me
in with everyone else!

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:26.650
You just wanted some money to
treat those local boys, didn't you?

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:30.850
They only care about how
deep your pockets are!

00:06:30.850 --> 00:06:32.230
Shut up!

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:36.850
Hey, what's wrong?!

00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:44.100
Three... Four...

00:06:45.310 --> 00:06:49.310
Five... Six...

00:06:49.310 --> 00:06:52.480
Seven... Eight...

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:54.850
Nine...

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:02.730
Once he wakes up, have him drink this.

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:03.900
Got it.

00:07:13.940 --> 00:07:15.230
Sachio...

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:20.980
I... I have to go...

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:27.020
They're waiting for me... They're...

00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:28.350
It's all right.

00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:16.900
Tastes like shit.

00:08:16.900 --> 00:08:19.810
Come on! Hurry up!

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:21.230
Toss them over here, too!

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:25.190
Okay! Welcome back, everyone!

00:08:35.230 --> 00:08:37.440
Looks like you're awake.

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:39.770
Well? How're you feeling?

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:43.020
I'm good. Sorry for troubling you.

00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:46.440
You just keeled over,
so you gave me a scare.

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:49.560
You've been through some
hard times, haven't you?

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:52.190
It's gonna be a while longer
till your bike's fixed up,

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:55.060
so go ahead and use
this trailer until then.

00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:57.150
But this is someone's...

00:08:57.150 --> 00:09:00.810
Oh, it's fine. He's rarely home.

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:05.440
That's why I occasionally let
some fresh air in and clean.

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:12.150
By the way, today's our yearly festival.

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:14.730
To make sure that our
departed family and friends

00:09:14.730 --> 00:09:17.400
don't lose their way coming back here,

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:21.850
we use flower petals to
create a path for them.

00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:28.350
I'm Marla. Let me know
if you need anything.

00:09:28.350 --> 00:09:31.100
It's the least I can do after
what my fool of a son did.

00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:32.850
Son?

00:09:32.850 --> 00:09:34.190
Ah...

00:09:34.190 --> 00:09:35.850
Bingo.

00:09:35.850 --> 00:09:37.690
Who the hell are you?!

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:43.230
We're paying money to stay here!

00:09:43.230 --> 00:09:44.770
Well, I'm sure you've been informed that

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:48.980
the landowner has passed,
so the land is going up for auction.

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:51.190
Where can we even go?

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:51.770
Get the hell outta here!

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:54.770
You'll have to figure
that out on your own.

00:09:54.770 --> 00:09:55.980
Begin.

00:10:03.690 --> 00:10:04.900
You're in the way!

00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:12.730
You're--

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:15.230
Looks like you're doing better.

00:10:15.230 --> 00:10:17.350
Apparently, that herbal tea did its job.

00:10:22.900 --> 00:10:25.730
There's still some time
before the auction.

00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:30.100
Barging in here like that is unnecessary
when we can settle things peacefully.

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:32.560
You're the ones making this difficult.

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:36.560
Well, the harder you push,
the harder we push back.

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:39.690
Today's a very important day for us.

00:10:39.690 --> 00:10:42.600
Can't you let us just enjoy the day?

00:10:45.190 --> 00:10:48.020
The auction is in two weeks.

00:10:48.020 --> 00:10:51.690
After that, you will all be
considered illegal occupants.

00:10:51.690 --> 00:10:53.770
That is all. Let's go.

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:10.980
Who do they think they are?
Illegal occupants, my ass!

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:16.900
Well, they've got a point.
We don't own this land.

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:19.480
Why are you guys so
attached to this place?

00:11:19.480 --> 00:11:21.770
Let's just get the hell outta here.

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:23.850
Mio, will you just--

00:11:27.690 --> 00:11:29.690
Mio might be right, though.

00:11:29.690 --> 00:11:31.520
Don't worry.

00:11:31.520 --> 00:11:34.100
I'm gonna buy this land.

00:11:34.100 --> 00:11:37.810
And Chief is spewing his
empty promises again.

00:11:37.810 --> 00:11:40.350
You're all talk.

00:11:40.350 --> 00:11:44.190
Well, I always try to solve
problems with my words first.

00:11:44.190 --> 00:11:47.150
And that's why you're
always losing your matches.

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:53.940
All right, let's get back to
work preparing this festival.

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:56.980
Once it gets dark, the dead's
gonna lose their way.

00:12:00.850 --> 00:12:05.060
<i>Mi casa es su casa.</i>

00:12:05.060 --> 00:12:08.310
It means "my house is your house."

00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:13.440
And this is our home.

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:12.520
Back where we're from,
we'd decorate with cockscomb flowers,

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:14.560
but they're hard to come by here.

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:25.520
My bad. I guess I took your bed.

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:28.770
Nah, it's fine. I've got that over there.

00:13:29.850 --> 00:13:35.520
I have a place to go home to,
so I don't care where I am.

00:13:44.350 --> 00:13:47.270
Me being a former Megalo-boxer is a lie.

00:13:47.270 --> 00:13:49.810
So that means you being ranked is also...

00:13:49.810 --> 00:13:52.600
That title pays the bills, you see.

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:58.980
Back there, you asked me if I
was embarrassed with myself.

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:04.190
We didn't come to this country to die.

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:08.560
This is to survive. There's nothing
embarrassing about surviving.

00:14:11.150 --> 00:14:14.650
When did you figure out who I was?

00:14:14.650 --> 00:14:18.690
Oh, from the start.
My son was a huge fan of yours.

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:26.560
"Gearless" Joe... was our star of hope.

00:14:27.730 --> 00:14:31.850
You went into that ring without
any Gear and became the champ.

00:14:33.270 --> 00:14:35.060
Which means we should be able to

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:37.900
start anew in a new land,
even if we don't have anything.

00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:40.480
That's what we kept telling ourselves from

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:43.560
the bottom of a very dark
boat as we came here.

00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:47.770
But all that was waiting
for us was a harsh reality.

00:14:47.770 --> 00:14:50.770
We're worked to the bone like
slaves for next to nothing

00:14:50.770 --> 00:14:55.060
and the locals called us
parasites who stole their jobs.

00:14:56.310 --> 00:15:01.560
We finally found our safe haven
in this abandoned amusement park.

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:04.480
And now, they're trying
to kick us out of here, too.

00:15:07.150 --> 00:15:08.850
"Gearless" Joe...

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:17.770
But I still haven't woken up from
this dream that you showed us.

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:23.980
There's a huge tournament in town soon.

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:27.900
I'm gonna win that and then buy this land.

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:30.810
Not that any of them are gonna believe me.

00:15:31.940 --> 00:15:35.440
You can dream all you want.

00:15:35.440 --> 00:15:39.400
But are you sure you're willing
to lose everything for that?

00:15:41.230 --> 00:15:45.480
It's already done,
so it doesn't concern me.

00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:50.060
Where are you headed next?

00:15:50.060 --> 00:15:54.560
Who knows? Unlike you,
I don't have a home to go back to.

00:15:58.900 --> 00:16:03.150
If you keep fighting like this,
you really will die.

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:04.350
I know.

00:16:08.020 --> 00:16:10.190
May I have this dance, Miss?

00:16:11.100 --> 00:16:13.350
Oh, quit it, you drunk.

00:16:25.690 --> 00:16:27.690
Damn it...

00:16:27.690 --> 00:16:29.060
Hey.

00:16:29.060 --> 00:16:30.690
Oh, Mio.

00:16:30.690 --> 00:16:32.600
Hey, we were worried about you.

00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:37.690
Give me a break. You guys suck.
You left my ass there and ran.

00:16:37.690 --> 00:16:42.350
What? That's not true. We were just
getting some weapons. Right?

00:16:42.350 --> 00:16:44.100
Yeah, exactly.

00:16:44.100 --> 00:16:45.850
Who the hell is that?

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:49.560
Oh, this is Mio. He's one of our buds.

00:16:49.560 --> 00:16:52.150
Buds? With him?

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:57.060
Hey, Mio, greet him. This is Tatsu.
He takes good care of us.

00:16:57.060 --> 00:16:58.230
Hey.

00:16:58.230 --> 00:17:02.150
So what's the deal with that dude?

00:17:02.150 --> 00:17:07.440
The second round's just begun,
but is it already pretty much over?

00:17:04.060 --> 00:17:05.310
Well, you see...

00:17:16.940 --> 00:17:19.770
Sorry for the trouble we caused you.

00:17:19.770 --> 00:17:21.560
It's all right.

00:17:21.560 --> 00:17:27.600
And here. I don't know if it's
enough to buy new Gear, but...

00:17:27.600 --> 00:17:30.060
...this is all I can afford right now.

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:34.520
It was nearing the end
of its rope, anyway.

00:17:34.520 --> 00:17:37.100
Not to mention, you took care of me.

00:17:37.100 --> 00:17:38.560
You already returned the favor.

00:17:42.310 --> 00:17:46.060
"Only do bad deeds for good."

00:17:46.060 --> 00:17:47.940
Words from back home.

00:17:47.940 --> 00:17:50.230
Don't forget that.

00:17:50.230 --> 00:17:51.480
Yeah.

00:18:01.690 --> 00:18:02.940
Where'd that guy go?

00:18:02.940 --> 00:18:05.020
He left.

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:07.230
Why didn't you stop him?!

00:18:34.350 --> 00:18:36.770
Heya, Chief.

00:18:36.770 --> 00:18:41.690
Mr. Hikawa. I'm pretty sure we told
you that we weren't leaving just yet.

00:18:41.690 --> 00:18:48.100
That's not why I'm here today. I heard
that you've got a rather unusual guest.

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:50.810
A guest? And who might that be?

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:53.600
Cut the crap!

00:18:53.600 --> 00:18:57.810
"Gearless" Joe.
I'm a huge fan of his, you see.

00:18:57.810 --> 00:19:02.100
I figured the audience would be
thrilled to see him in the tournament.

00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:03.730
"Gearless" Joe?

00:19:03.730 --> 00:19:05.600
That was Joe?

00:19:05.600 --> 00:19:07.100
The commerce and industry guys

00:19:07.100 --> 00:19:10.190
would also like him to participate
to help liven up the town.

00:19:10.190 --> 00:19:14.060
Whaddya say, Chief?
Won't you let us talk to him?

00:19:14.060 --> 00:19:15.850
Of course, we won't forget to thank you.

00:19:15.850 --> 00:19:22.560
We can even talk to the right people
to delay the auction on this place.

00:19:22.560 --> 00:19:25.600
Well, that's too bad, truly.

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:28.350
You got here a bit too late.

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:31.190
"Gearless" Joe isn't here anymore.

00:19:31.190 --> 00:19:33.230
He's not here?

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:34.810
That little shit!

00:19:38.650 --> 00:19:42.150
Though the situation wouldn't
change even if he were here.

00:19:42.150 --> 00:19:45.270
Hm? What do you mean?

00:19:45.270 --> 00:19:50.150
I'm going to enter that tournament.
The paperwork's already done.

00:19:50.150 --> 00:19:51.600
You?

00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:55.060
You finally lose your marbles getting
knocked in the head too many times?

00:19:55.060 --> 00:19:58.270
You're just phony who gets
knocked around in fixed fights.

00:19:58.270 --> 00:20:00.520
Well, I need money...

00:20:00.520 --> 00:20:03.020
...so that I can buy this land.

00:20:05.480 --> 00:20:09.940
I see. Then I guess
we're done talking here.

00:20:11.900 --> 00:20:15.560
I'll be praying for you on the DL.

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:22.150
Chief...

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:23.940
What are you thinking?

00:20:45.190 --> 00:20:50.100
But I still haven't woken up from
this dream that you showed us.

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:58.520
First, we gotta get you some new Gear.

00:20:58.520 --> 00:21:01.980
You can't go in there
without it anymore, can ya?

00:21:10.100 --> 00:21:12.060
Hey, Pops...

00:21:14.310 --> 00:21:17.900
I'm the one who killed you, aren't I?

00:21:17.900 --> 00:21:21.310
Yeah, you sure the hell did, kid.

00:21:35.940 --> 00:21:38.520
Well, Partner...

00:21:38.520 --> 00:21:40.520
Where're we off to next?

00:22:02.770 --> 00:22:05.440
You forget something, Joe?

00:22:05.440 --> 00:22:10.850
You said you still haven't woken up
from this dream yet, right?

00:22:10.850 --> 00:22:12.520
Yeah.

00:22:12.520 --> 00:22:17.310
I guess I wanna see how that dream ends.

00:22:17.310 --> 00:22:18.850
Will you let me help you?

00:22:24.600 --> 00:22:29.650
I appreciate the offer, but I'll
only accept on one condition.

00:22:29.650 --> 00:22:30.850
I know.

00:22:37.020 --> 00:22:38.850
The drugs are gone.
